1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,271
I think it's only right to start off with christmas pantoimes how do you even describe a british christmas pantoime to someone who has no knowledge of the concept.
我觉得先讲圣诞哑剧才对。可怎么向完全不懂这个概念的人解释英式圣诞哑剧呢？

2
00:00:13,281 --> 00:00:24,400
How it's like a very chaotic children's play but it also is very much for adults as well and everyone is screaming.
它就像一出非常混乱的儿童剧，但也很适合大人看，而且全场都在大喊。

3
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:33,841
This is something that I had never heard of in canada I've never seen anything in canada I don't even think in north america as a whole we have any sort of equivalent.
这种东西我在加拿大从没听过，也没见过；我甚至觉得，整个北美都没有对应的表演。

4
00:00:33,841 --> 00:00:48,321
It's just like something that is so uniquely british and strange and wonderful and chaotic and funny and wholesome and risier and strange have I said strange yet.
它就是特别英式、奇怪、美妙、混乱、好笑、温馨，还带点大胆。我已经说过“奇怪”了吗？

5
00:00:48,321 --> 00:01:01,281
But also wonderful it is very much a theatrical contradiction for both children and adults wholesome and risque it's just there's nothing else like it.
但它也很美妙：给孩子和大人看，既温馨又大胆，简直是舞台上的矛盾体，没有别的东西像它。

6
00:01:01,281 --> 00:01:08,481
Number two something I've noticed here in the uk is that the brits have a very strong opinion on when the tree goes up.
第二个，我在英国注意到，大家对什么时候摆圣诞树很有意见。

7
00:01:08,481 --> 00:01:16,961
And no matter which date you choose to put your tree up you are wrong I get into trouble with this every year.
而且不管你选哪天摆树，你都是错的。我每年都会因为这件事惹来意见。

8
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:24,640
If you want to annoy a british person tell them you're going to put your tree up in november they will act like you have killed their child.
想惹英国人不高兴，就说你打算十一月摆树；按她的夸张说法，他们会反应得像遭遇了极大的悲剧。

9
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:33,201
I know there are historical and like religious connotations on when the tree is supposed to go up spoiler alert I don't care.
我知道，树应该什么时候摆，背后有历史和宗教方面的含义。不过提前透露一下：我不在乎。

10
00:01:33,201 --> 00:01:40,641
I think november in England is so dull and gray and miserable and I've got this cute little tree that I could put up.
我觉得英国的十一月又阴沉、又灰暗、又难熬，而我正好有棵可爱的小树可以摆出来。

11
00:01:40,641 --> 00:01:47,841
I already have all the bits for it I could put it up in november I could put the lights on and it's cozy and it's nice I'm going to do it.
装饰品我都有；我可以十一月就摆树、开灯，温馨又舒服，那我就这么做。

12
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:57,841
Number three of british christmas traditions we have christmas crackers and very specifically wearing the crown from the cracker.
第三个英式圣诞传统是拉炮，尤其是戴上拉炮里面的纸王冠。

13
00:01:57,841 --> 00:02:06,240
Whether you are posh or not posh it is a right of passage um I went to like quite a fancy christmas dinner.
无论你讲不讲究身份，这都是一个必经环节。嗯，我曾经去过一次挺讲究的圣诞晚餐。

14
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:14,800
One time like we're talking waitros products do you know what I mean and everybody pulled their christmas cracker and everyone took turns sharing the little joke.
讲究到什么程度呢？她拿超市品牌开了个玩笑。大家拉开圣诞拉炮，轮流念里面的小笑话。

15
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:21,601
And then everyone put on their crown it's just you have to there's no question of it you're going to wear the crown.
然后大家都戴上王冠。就是得戴，没有商量余地，你肯定要戴。

16
00:02:21,601 --> 00:02:27,281
We never had christmas crackers um at christmas dinner in canada it was just not something that we did.
我们在加拿大吃圣诞晚餐时从没有拉炮；这就不是我们家的习惯。

17
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:35,361
Um and it's so fun here where it's not even a question like there are going to be crackers you're going to pull them you're going to wear the crown.
我觉得这里好玩的是，大家根本不用讨论：一定有拉炮，一定会拉，也一定会戴王冠。

18
00:02:35,361 --> 00:02:49,201
Which christmas carol is about an animal with three legs I don't know little wonky and I don't know what this is.
哪首圣诞颂歌唱的是三条腿的动物？我不知道。她念出小笑话后又说，我也不知道这是什么。

19
00:02:49,201 --> 00:02:57,121
Number four a very strange british christmas tradition obsession with adverts but of course the christmas variety.
第四个：一种很奇特的英国圣诞习惯，对广告着迷，当然是圣诞广告这一类。

20
00:02:57,121 --> 00:03:01,921
This is something I have fully embraced I refuse to watch an advert.
这件事我已经完全接受了。不过平时我可拒绝看广告。

21
00:03:01,921 --> 00:03:08,080
The other day um I have amazon prime just for the deliveries I don't really watch stuff on amazon prime.
前几天，嗯，我订 Amazon Prime 只是为了配送，其实不怎么看上面的节目。

22
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:13,361
But I was on it for some reason I think this was when I was ill a couple weeks ago and I was looking for something to watch.
但不知怎么，我当时在用它，应该是几周前生病时，在找点东西看。

23
00:03:13,361 --> 00:03:19,281
I found something I watched it right I watched it I watched it for a couple of minutes I pay for amazon prime.
我找到一部片子，就看了，真的看了，大概看了几分钟；而且我还付了订阅费。

24
00:03:19,281 --> 00:03:28,080
And then I get hit with three minutes of unskippable ads I closed it I didn't watch it anymore I refuse.
结果我迎面碰上三分钟不能跳过的广告。我关掉了，不看了，我拒绝看。

25
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:33,440
But there's something about british christmas adverts that are so fun to watch.
不过英国圣诞广告有种特别之处，让人看着很开心。

26
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:43,041
There's so much effort that goes into them and planning and budget and every year there are like standouts that I actually remember the following year.
制作它们投入了很多努力、策划和预算；每年总有一些特别出色的广告，我到第二年还记得。

27
00:03:43,041 --> 00:03:54,321
Like that is so strange to remember a commercial an advert it's crazy I reacted to this year's christmas adverts that video got copyright blocked unfortunately.
居然会记得一则广告，真奇妙。我做了今年圣诞广告的反应视频，可惜那个视频被版权限制了。

28
00:03:54,321 --> 00:03:59,761
So big rip don't earn anything from that one but it was really fun to make anyway so who cares.
所以挺遗憾的，那个视频没赚到什么钱。不过制作过程很有趣，那又有什么关系呢？

29
00:03:59,761 --> 00:04:08,801
But in particular there was an ad that was like decent you know I'm watching it I'm making jokes and stuff and it actually made me cry.
其中有一则广告本来还不错，我一边看一边开玩笑，结果它真的把我看哭了。

30
00:04:08,801 --> 00:04:16,801
And then when I was editing that video I cried again like they are really well done not all of them most of them are very well done.
后来剪那段视频时，我又哭了一次。那些广告做得真好；也不是每则都好，但大多数确实不错。

31
00:04:16,801 --> 00:04:20,881
Very interesting memorable that you actually talk about with people.
很有趣，很令人难忘，你甚至真的会和别人聊起它们。

32
00:04:20,881 --> 00:04:27,120
You remember them the years um as they go by you know what I'm trying to say previous you remember the previous ones.
年头过去了，你还记得它们，你懂我意思吧？以前的——你会记得以前那些广告。

33
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:38,960
Which I couldn't tell you a single advert that I remember of the last like five years I just you don't they're not memorable does that make sense.
但过去大约五年里的一般广告，我一则都说不上来；就是记不住，它们不够难忘。这样说能明白吗？

34
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:43,120
I feel like I've been talking about christmas adverts for a long time I just love them I think they're great.
我感觉圣诞广告已经讲了很久了。我就是喜欢，觉得它们很棒。

35
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:49,601
You do not get this in canada you do not get this in america it is just wonderful.
按她的经验，加拿大没有这种体验，美国也没有；她觉得这太美妙了。
